fix: resolve all 16 audit findings — the bridge is a client, not a pipe

The bridge was written as a pipe, but the thing on either end is a protocol with
a session, a content-negotiation contract, and concurrent in-flight requests. The
body is still forwarded byte-for-byte — that invariant is the design — but the
transport around it now honours those three.

High:
- #1 concurrent dispatch with an inflight ceiling of 8 and an EOF drain. A 40s
  Monte Carlo no longer delays a 50ms bracket lookup behind it by 40 seconds.
- #2 AbortController + NUMERATICA_TIMEOUT_MS. Node's fetch has no default
  timeout, so a slept laptop or dropped VPN wedged the process permanently with
  stdin held open — the one failure shape no client heuristic detects.
- #3 Accept now lists text/event-stream as the spec requires. This only worked
  because our own server is lenient; a compliant one may answer 406.
- #4 MCP-Session-Id captured and echoed, plus the 404 re-initialize path.
- #5 MCP-Protocol-Version sent, taken from the negotiated initialize result.
- #6 SSE bodies parsed per frame. They previously failed JSON.parse and fell
  through to oneLine, which faithfully emitted "event: message data: {...}" to
  stdout — silent on this side, which is why it looked like it worked.

Medium/low: #7 exitCode instead of exit() (async stdout is not flushed by
exit()); #8 retry on 429/502/503/504 honouring Retry-After, inside the timeout
budget; #9 backpressure-aware serialized writer; #10 --key-file plus a README
caveat, since a key in argv is visible to ps; #11 --key=value, the form that
silently fell through to "NUMERATICA_API_KEY is required" while the key was on
the command line; #12 DELETE the session on shutdown; #13 truncate on code
points, not UTF-16 units; #14 reject batches explicitly; #15 comment pinning why
id===undefined is the notification test.

#16: 8 tests -> 40, and mockResponse now carries real headers, which is what made
#4 and #5 invisible before. CI matrices 20/22/24 and the engines floor moves to
20 (18 is EOL and was never exercised). prepublishOnly gates publish on green.

Each fix was verified by reverting it and confirming the suite fails. That found
a bug in one of the new tests: #13's fixture used 600 emoji, and a 500-unit cut
across two-unit characters lands exactly on a pair boundary, so it never split
one. Fixed with a one-character offset.

Smoke-tested against production: initialize negotiates 2025-11-25, tools/list
returns 76 tools, every frame single-line, clean exit.

The audit is committed alongside, marked resolved.

